# What never enters a Docker build context (ADR-0059). The three Dockerfiles `COPY . .` into
# their build stage, so without this file every build would carry the workstation's .env, a
# runner's deploy key, a gigabyte of host node_modules and yesterday's dist into a layer.
# The runtime images copy only what the build stage produced, and CI builds from a clean
# checkout; this makes a workstation build the same build.

# Secrets and keys. The build gets what it needs as build args and BuildKit secrets.
.env
.env.*
.env-use
.deploy/
**/*.pem
**/id_ed25519*

# Version control, CI, editors, agents.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Installed and generated on the host; the image installs and builds its own.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/coverage/
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
**/*.log
.turbo/
**/.turbo/

# Local state and scratch, never part of the product.
.pen-data/
tasks/
docs/
*.html
